es maliciosas, sino decisiones basadas en criterios legales.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en años distintos. Analizar si los contratos junto al límite se ajustan a presupuestos cerrados o a criterios de mercado.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 22 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 2.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 11.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.0 to 26.0. December accounts for 0% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 10. Contract [1], for 37,740.85 euros, was awarded in June 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove misconduct. It could reflect market conditions or budget constraints. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate improper actions by the body or its contractors.\nWhat can be checked: Check the awardee A's contracts for repeated purchases of similar services. Review contract [1] to see if the amount is consistent with market rates. Look for patterns in the timing of contracts to determine if they were planned or reactive.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["AmbkIpGJIIaOUi78BmzhOQ%3D%3D","PzbGUkrhVBaTylGzYmBF9Q%3D%3D","5PpnaHmjdFES7pcxhTeWOg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}